{"id":"word:hebrew:H410","type":"word","title":"אֵל","subtitle":"H410 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"strength ; as adjective, mighty ; especially the Almighty (but used also of any deity )","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֵל (H410) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 245 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֵל (ʼêl) means strength ; as adjective, mighty ; especially the Almighty (but used also of any deity ) First listed occurrence: 1Sam 2 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֵל","transliteration":"ʼêl","pronunciation":"ale","strong":"H410","lemmaId":"hebrew:H410","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אֵ֑ל","אֵ֣ל","אֵֽל","אֵ֥ל","אֵ֖ל"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",139],["HNcmsc",21],["HTd/Ncmsa",19],["HRd/Ncmsa",12],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",12],["HR/Ncmsa",11],["HR/Ncmsc",9],["HNcmpa",4],["HC/Ncmsa",4],["HNp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"strength ; as adjective, mighty ; especially the Almighty (but used also of any deity )","usage":"God (god), × goodly, × great, idol, might(-y one), power, strong. Compare names in '-el.'","full":"H410. el II. אֵל god , אֶלְדָּעָה אֶלְדָּד, etc. see I. אלה . II. אֵל noun masculine (also, in proper name אֱלִי אֶל, ; Samaritan אל , Phoenician אלן אל, (i.e. probably אֵלֹן ), Sabean אל , DHM Or. Congr. Leiden, 1883 , Assyrian ilu , Dl w ; perhaps also Arabic, Aramaic compare Nö on the passage ; on goddess אלת Phoenician, Palmyrene, Nabataean, Sabean (also אלהת ) DHM l. c ; Arabic (plural ) Fl Kl. Schr. i. 154 , Assyrian Allatu Jr 66 , Syriac , compare also Bae Rel 58, 90, 97, 271, 207 ) god, but with various subordinate applications to express idea of might; &#8212; hardly ever in prose except with defining word (adjective or Genitive); its only suffix is יִ֯ ; — 1 applied to men of might and rank , גוים אֵל mighty one of the nations Ezek 31:11 (of Nebuchadnezzar; ᵐ5 ἄρχων ἔθνων , איל some MSS. Co); אֵלִים mighty men Job 41:17 ( אילים , many MSS. Di); גִבּוֺרִים אֵלֵי mighty heroes Ezek 32:21 ( אֵילֵי MSS. Co); הָאֶרֶץ אֵילֵי 17:13 ; 2Kin 24:15 (Kt אולי ); אֵילִים Exod 15:15 (probably plural of III. אַיִל , q. v.) These readings are uncertain because of an effort to distinguish these forms from the divine name. גִּבּוֺר אֵל mighty hero (as above) or divine hero (as reflecting the divine majesty) Isa 9:6 . 2 angels , אֵלִים בְּנֵי Psa 29:1 ; 89:7 = הָאֱלֹהִים בְּנֵי . 3 gods of the nations , אֵלִים אֵל God of gods , supreme God Dan 11:36 ; בָּאֵלִם כָמֹכָה מִי who is like thee among the gods Exod 15:11 ; idols Isa 43:10 ; 44:10 , 15 , 17 ; 46:6 ; בשמים אל מי what God in heaven Deut 3:24 ; אחר אֵל another god Exod 34:14 (J); זר אֵל foreign god Psa 44:21 ; 81:10 ; נכר אל Deut 32:12 ; Mal 2:11 ; Psa 81:10 . 4 El proper name ברית אל El Berith Judg 9:46 (= ברית בעל 8:33 ; 9:4 ) compare also 6 ( f ) below 5 as characterizing mighty things in nature , אל חררי mighty mountains Psa 36:7 (literally mountains of El ); also 50:10 Ol Bi Che see below II. אלף ; אל ארזי mighty cedars 80:11 ; אל כוכבי lofty stars Isa 14:13 . 6 God 217 , the one only and true God of Israel: ( a ) הָאֵל the God, the true God Gen 31:13 ; 35:1 , 3 ; 46:3 (E) 2Sam 22:31 , 33 , 48 (= Psa 18:31 ; 18:33 ; 18:48 ) 68:20 ; 68:21 ; 77:15 ; הַנֶּאֱמָן הָאֵל the faithful God Deut 7:9 ; הגדול האל the great God 10:17 = Jer 32:18 ; Dan 9:4 ; Neh 1:5 ; 9:32 ; הקדשׁ האל the holy God Isa 5:17 ; יהוה האל the God Yahweh 42:5 ; Psa 85:9 . ( b ) אֵלִי my God Exod 15:2 (poetry) Psa 18:3 ; 22:2 (twice in verse); 22:11 ; 63:2 ; 68:25 ; 89:27 ; 102:25 ; 118:28 ; 140:7 ; Isa 44:17 . ( c ) construct אל בית אל the God of Bethel , who had his seat there Gen 35:7 (E); אביך אל God of thy fathers 49:25 (poetry); ישראל אל Psalm 68:36; יעקב אל Psa 146:5 ; השמים אל the God of heaven 136:26 ; סלעי אל the God who is my rock 42:10 ; גילי שמחת אל the God who is the joy of my exultation 43:4 ; רֳאִי אֵל the God who lets himself be seen Gen 16:13 (J); הכבוד אל the God of glory Psa 29:3 ; דעות אל the all-knowing God 1Sam 2:3 (poetry); עוֺלָם אֵל the everlasting God Gen 21:33 (J); ישועתי אל Isa 12:2 ; חַיָּ֑י אל Psa 42:9 ; אמת אל 31:6 = אֱמוּנָה אל Deut 32:4 (poetry); נקמות אל Psa 94:1 (twice in verse); גְּמֻלוֺת אל Jer 51:56 . ( d ) אֶחָד אל one God Mal 2:10 ; גדול אל a great God Deut 7:21 ; Psa 77:14 ; 95:3 ; מסתתר אל a God hiding himself Isa 45:15 ; רחום אל a compassionate God Exod 34:6 (J) Deut 4:31 ; Psa 86:15 ; נשא אל a forgiving God 99:8 ; חַנּוּן אל a gracious God Neh 9:31 ; Jonah 4:2 ; קנא אל a jealous God Exod 20:5 ; 34:14 (J) Deut 4:24 ; 5:9 ; 6:15 ; Josh 24:19 (D) = קנוא אל Nahum 1:2 ; חי אֵל a living God Josh 3:10 (J) Hosea 2:1 ; Psa 42:3 ; 84:3 ; צדיק אל Isa 45:21 ; רשע חפץ אֵל לא Psa 5:5 ; אֵל לא Deut 32:21 (poetry) Isa 31:3 ; Ezek 28:2 (twice in verse); 28:9 ; כמוךָ אל מי Micah 7:18 (compare Exod 15:11 ). ( e ) God (the only true God, needing no article or predicate to define him) Num 12:13 (E read אַל Di) always in poetry, Job 5:8 + (55 t. Job), Psa 7:12 ; 10:11-12 , 16:1 ; 17:6 ; 19:1 ; 52:3 , 7 ; 55:20 ; 57:3 ; 73:11 , 17 ; 74:8 ; 77:10 ; 78:7-8 , 18 , 19 , 34 , 41 ; 82:1 ; 83:2 ; 90:2 ; 104:21 ; 106:14 , 21 ; 107:11 ; 118:27 ; 139:17 , 23 ; 149:6 ; 150:1 ; Isa 40:18 ; 43:12 ; 45:14 , 20 ; 46:9 ; Lam 3:41 ; Hosea 11:9 ; 12:1 ; Mal 1:9 ; עִמָּנוּאל God is with us , as name of child in prediction Isa 7:14 ; compare 8:8 , 10 . ( f ) El, a divine name ישראל אלהי אל Gen 33:20 (E); הרוחות אלהי אל Num 16:22 (P = הרוחות אלהי יהוה 27:16 ); יהוה אלהים אל Josh 22:22 (P) Psa 50:1 . This is probable also in the ancient poems, Num 23:8 , 19 , 22 , 23 ; 24:4 , 8 , 16 , 23 (poetry Balaam || שדּי & עליון ) Deut 32:18 ; 33:26 (poetry Moses || צוּר & קֶדֶם אֱלֹהֵי ) 2Sam 22:32 ; 23:5 (poetry David || צוּר ) and in the combinations עליון אל (5 t.; see עליון ) & שדּי אל (10 t.; see שַׁדַּי ). 7 אֵל strength, power (on connection with I. אָלָה compare Di Gen 1:1 ; 31:29 ) in יָדִי יֶשׁלְֿאֵל it is according to the power of my hand = it is in my power, etc. 31:29 (E; followed by לְ + Infinitive); יָדְ֯יךָ לְאֵל בִּהְיוֺת Prov 3:27 (followed by id.); יָדָם יֶשׁלְֿאֵל Micah 2:1 ; (absolute); negative יָדֶ֑ךָ לְאֵל וְאֵין Deut 28:32 (absolute) = thou shalt be powerless , so Neh 5:5 . **See also Brock ZAW xxvi (1906). 29 ff. (meaning 'might' very dubious: renders belongs to the god of (my) hand , supposing phrase a survival, with original meaning forgotten, of ancient idea, found also among other nations, of spirits conferring powers upon particular members of body).","rootNote":"shortened from 352 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 2 3","keyReferences":["1Sam 2 3","2Sam 2 30","2Sam 22 31","2Sam 22 32","2Sam 22 33","2Sam 22 48","2Sam 23 5","Dan 9 4"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":245,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 2 3","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֤ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"2Sam 2 30","book":"2Sam","chapter":2,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵֽל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"2Sam 22 31","book":"2Sam","chapter":22,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֵ֖ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 22 32","book":"2Sam","chapter":22,"verse":32,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֖ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 22 33","book":"2Sam","chapter":22,"verse":33,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֵ֥ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 22 48","book":"2Sam","chapter":22,"verse":48,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֵ֕ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Sam 23 5","book":"2Sam","chapter":23,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֵ֑ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"Dan 9 4","book":"Dan","chapter":9,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הָ/אֵ֤ל","source